  "worked_solution": "Writing the terms of the series explicitly, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=3(x+2)-\\frac{9}{2}(x+2)^{2}+⋯+{{(-1)^{n+1}\\frac{{3}^{n}}{n}(x+2)^{n}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{the }n\\text{th term}}+⋯.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above series term-by-term gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=3-9(x+2)+⋯+{{(-1)^{n+1}{3}^{n}(x+2)^{n-1}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{the }n\\text{th term}}+⋯.\n$$\n\nWe can now write the Taylor series for ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the sigma notation as follows:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{3}^{n}(-1)^{n+1}(x+2)^{n-1}\n$$",
